# .airules — Binding specification for any agent working on this repo
# Read this file IN FULL before any task. Re-read after any schema or
# dependency change.

## 1. Agent operating rules
- Capabilities (verified 2026-09-29): the agent has a sandboxed Linux
  shell with git and network READ access to this repo. It does NOT
  have a Flutter SDK, Android SDK, or any device — it cannot build or
  run the app; the human is the only verifier. GitHub tokens pasted
  into chat or committed anywhere are auto-revoked by secret scanning
  within minutes (observed twice). Github tokens should be found in Environment variables. 
  Report if the github token is not working. 
- Always `git pull`/fetch origin main before reading code; your local
  copy may be stale. Report discrepancies between this file and the
  tree instead of silently "fixing" either one.
- Inspect the project file structure first, then read this file fully.
- Never guess package API signatures. If uncertain, ask the human to
  paste the exact analyzer error or the IDE IntelliSense candidates.
- Pre-emptively declare every import and pub dependency a change needs.
- Prefer full-file replacements for edited files.
- The analyzer message is the specification. Adapt code to installed
  versions; never argue with them.
- Request log tails, not summaries, when diagnosing failures.

## 2. Project overview
Offline-first personal wargaming rules compendium ("Rules Repository").
Hierarchy: Game -> Folder (arbitrary depth, optional) -> Book (PDF).
No network calls at runtime, ever. Online content enters only via
user-imported files or (planned) pasted text.

## 3. Stack and pins (CURRENT — re-verified against pubspec.yaml +
##    settings.gradle.kts at commit 7c8f716, 2026-09-29)
- Flutter on a recent SDK (post-3.41: cacheExtent deprecated in favor
  of scrollCacheExtent).
- sqflite ^2.3.0 + path ^1.8.3 + path_provider ^2.1.0 for storage and
  database; sqflite_common_ffi ^2.3.0 for desktop FFI.
- PDF stack (pure-Dart; pdfx REMOVED): pdf ^3.11.0 + printing ^5.13.0
  via lib/services/pdf_backend.dart / pdf_backend_dart.dart. History
  note: pdfx was tried first and reverted — its bundled Android PDFium
  Gradle subproject does not build under AGP 9. Do NOT re-add pdfx.
- file_picker: ^8.3.1. 8.x hard-codes compileSdk android-34, which
  trips ":file_picker:checkDebugAarMetadata" because
  flutter_plugin_android_lifecycle (transitive) requires API 36. This
  is HANDLED by the compileSdk patcher in android/build.gradle.kts
  (forces every com.android.library subproject to compileSdk >= 36),
  so pinning 8.3.1 is safe. If you bump file_picker to 10.x anyway,
  FilePicker.platform API is unchanged; keep the patcher regardless.
- Build chain (android/settings.gradle.kts + wrapper): AGP 9.0.1,
  Kotlin 2.3.20, Gradle 9.1.0. These are the versions Flutter stable
  validates; never downgrade this chain to "fix" a plugin problem —
  fix the plugin or the compileSdk patcher instead. NOTE: AGP 9
  removed BaseExtension.compileSdkVersion(int); the patcher must use
  LibraryExtension.compileSdk (String property).
- dart:io Platform for platform branching.

## 4. Database schema — CURRENT VERSION: 4
- games(id, name UNIQUE)
- folders(id, game_id FK cascade, parent_folder_id, name)
- books(id, game_id FK cascade, title, file_path,
        source_type DEFAULT 'pdf', last_page DEFAULT 1,
        folder_id NULL means game root)
- Migration chain lives in onUpgrade: v1->v2 source_type,
  v2->v3 last_page, v3->v4 folders + folder_id. Every future schema
  change MUST bump the version and extend onUpgrade. Never recreate
  tables; never drop user data.
- PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON is set in onConfigure.
- Book rows point at copied files inside app support, never originals.

## 5. Reader (single pure-Dart path on both platforms)
- Both Windows and Android use the custom lazy renderer (_PageImage in
  reader_screen.dart): ListView of pages, strictly serialized static
  render queue, per-document raster cache, 20s render timeout, zoom by
  re-rastering at width * factor, pinch via InteractiveViewer.
- pdfx PdfView is GONE; do not reintroduce it or PdfViewPinch (the old
  Windows PDFium deadlock note only ever applied to pdfx).
- _PageImageState MUST NOT touch MediaQuery (or any inherited widget)
  inside initState(); load from didChangeDependencies(). Regression
  seen on Fold5: "dependOnInheritedWidgetOfExactType<MediaQuery>() was
  called before initState() completed" red screen.
- Bottom bars need SafeArea(bottom): the Fold5 navigation bar covered
  import/create buttons until fixed in 7c8f716.
- Zoom percentages are integers, clamped 50..300.

## 6. Environment quirks (human's Windows machine)
- App support dir: %APPDATA%\com.example\<product>\ (the Windows runner
  CompanyName is com.example; books/ subdir holds imported PDFs).
  Do not "fix" this; the human accepts it.
- Android SDK at D:\Coding\Android SDK; adb at
  D:\Coding\Android SDK\platform-tools\adb.exe (not on PATH by default).
- C: drive is small — ALL caches/tooling live on D:. Flutter SDK
  D:\coding\flutter; Android Studio D:\Coding\Android studio; Gradle
  home GRADLE_USER_HOME=D:\Coding\DevCache\gradle;
  PUB_CACHE=D:\Coding\DevCache\flutterPubCache.
  Never suggest paths under %USERPROFILE% or C:\ for downloads/caches.
- System Java is JDK 25. Gradle 9.1.0 (the current wrapper) runs on it;
  do NOT downgrade Gradle to 8.x for any reason — Gradle 8.x rejects
  JDK 25. If a tool ever reports a Java/Gradle mismatch, align the
  wrapper to what Flutter validates rather than pinning
  org.gradle.java.home.
- Wireless ADB device id is NOT "SM-F946B"; use the full id shown by
  flutter devices (e.g. adb-RFCW70KTWDD-DpexMv._adb-tls-connect._tcp)
  or plain `flutter run` with the interactive picker.
- android/local.properties contains machine-absolute D: paths and is
  gitignored; never commit it and never assume its values in tracked files.
- sdkmanager.bat crashes (NTSTATUS 0xC0000409) under modern Java.
  NEVER invoke it. Install SDK components via Android Studio UI only.
- NDK pinned: ndkVersion = "30.0.16248370" in
  android/app/build.gradle.kts.
- Device: Samsung Fold5 (SM-F946B) via wireless ADB.
- Builds run from the VS Code terminal via flutter run.

## 7. Feature state
Done: game CRUD; folder tree of arbitrary depth; picker-first import
with filename-default naming and book rename; reader with continuous
scroll, page slider with scrub bubble, numeric jump, position memory;
Android zoom + pinch; pure-Dart pdf+printing backend on both platforms
(pdfx removed); Fold5 nav-bar SafeArea + MediaQuery initState crash fix.
Planned (design for these, do not build yet):
- FTS5 full-text search over extracted page text with scoped ranking
  (current book > game > global) and snippet() excerpts. UI slot:
  widgets/search_result_card.dart (empty placeholder). Note: the
  `pdf` package can extract embedded text per page (PdfDocument.pages
  .text), but scanned/image-only PDFs will yield nothing — design a
  graceful "no text layer" state.
- Chapter navigation via the document outline (package:pdf exposes
  outline/catalog), regex fallback for outline-less PDFs.
